# ==============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions (root context: apps/api and the bot worker)
# ==============================================================================
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Without it, `docker build .` uploaded a 2.6 GB build context on every single
# build: node_modules (1.2 GB), .venv (1.2 GB) and web/node_modules (145 MB).
# A hosted builder spends minutes receiving files before it compiles anything,
# and Railway's build step times out long before that finishes.
#
# The second, quieter problem was worse. `COPY . ./` in Dockerfile.bot and in
# web/Dockerfile copied the host's macOS node_modules *over* the Linux ones
# already installed inside the image. Native binaries compiled for darwin do
# not run on alpine, so the container died in ways that looked like application
# bugs rather than packaging mistakes.
#
# Dependencies are installed inside the image. They are never copied from here.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.venv
venv

# Secrets must never reach an image layer, even a private one. The platform
# injects these at runtime; the example files are kept so the list of required
# variables stays discoverable.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
*.pem
*.key

# Build output is produced inside the image, never shipped into it.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Not referenced by either image built from this context.
web
mobile
apps/web
ui-audit
ui-design
docs
.github

# Model weights and media.
*.pt
*.onnx
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.mp4

# Local tooling, editor state and OS noise.
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.workbuddy-ai
.claude
.gemini
.codex
.yolo_config
*.bak
*.log
